# femahoy chat: from request to mesh, solve and report

Source: femahoy at 321483d6, read only.
`daemon/` is `crates/fh/src/daemon/`.
Machine `chat` is the agent process in the daemon (`Log` in `daemon/chat.rs`): its state is not a field, but `running()` over the flags `reading`, `turn`, `sent`, `taken` and `input`.
Machine `job` is what the page shows for one request (`entry()` in `daemon/page.html`).
It is a parallel region of `chat`.

## Requirements

- R1: A message during the work reaches the agent at its next step.
  — DESIGN.md:36
- R2: `Stop agent and commands` ends the work at once.
  — DESIGN.md:36
- R3: If no agent is alive, a message starts one first, and the new agent continues the session of the chat.
  — daemon/chat.rs:238 and daemon/chat.rs:274
- R4: An `error` entry shows when the agent cannot start, or when it ended before the end of its work.
  — daemon/chat.rs:36
- R5: A status shows the current action of the agent and the time.
  — DESIGN.md:36
- R6: A missing or signed-out agent tells the person what to do.
  — DESIGN.md:82
- R7: The agent writes a CAD script for the part, meshes it with gmsh, writes the solver input and solves it.
  — README.md:42
- R8: It solves at least 2 meshes to find the mesh error.
  — README.md:42
- R9: At the end, the agent writes 1 HTML report with the results, a hand check and the viewer.
  — README.md:42
- R10: The page refuses an empty message.
  — daemon/chat.rs:242

## Bugs

- B1: After Stop, entries of the stopped agent still show.
  A late `end` entry hides the Rerun button (daemon/page.html:819).
  Row `* | stale_line`.
  — tests/chat_stale_line.rs fails on 321483d6

